comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-24T14:24:39.321Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-24: searched all statuses for health output cursor stale; dynamic telemetry continuation; declared row collection recovery; and read_output_cursor_stale. The nearest lineage is closed pm-8nev0o for missing continuation support and open pm-5t33or for budget contracts. Neither owns a cursor that is emitted successfully but invalid before its first use."
  "2026-08-24T16:39:11.627Z","harness:codex","Evidence 2026-08-24: both linked tests passed with trusted local-source provenance (10 transport tests plus 3 fingerprint tests); the temporary real-process CLI regression advances observation timestamps between pages and successfully replays the emitted cursor; substantive queue changes and non-health timestamp changes remain stale. Full 7,893-test suite and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage passed, along with contracts, SDK surface, static quality, lint, package-first dogfood, external-package, and packed npx acceptance."
  "2026-08-24T16:50:17.905Z","harness:codex","Review finding: Bugbot identified that the first implementation excluded only observation timestamps while enabled command telemetry can change queue counters and pending-span detail fields between health pages. Reopened to define a truthful dynamic-row snapshot contract and add telemetry-enabled real-process replay coverage before re-closing."
  "2026-08-24T17:02:11.742Z","harness:codex","Review correction evidence 2026-08-24: policy v2 publishes volatile_detail_row_names=[telemetry] and guarantee=nonvolatile_snapshot_and_row_identity. The real-process regression explicitly enables telemetry, forces queue retention through a local failing endpoint, verifies queued events exist after page one, and successfully resumes page two. Unit controls prove telemetry queue/pending-span detail churn resumes while storage evidence, telemetry verdicts, non-health fields, and policy-version drift fail closed. Linked tests passed 13/13; authoritative suite passed 572 files and 7,893 tests with exact 57,586/43,104/11,987/55,504 statement/branch/function/line coverage."
  "2026-08-24T17:16:32.184Z","harness:codex","Security Review finding: the dynamic-row exclusion was broader than the documented trust boundary. Correction scopes exclusions to explicit telemetry lifecycle counters/timestamps only; stable configuration, endpoint/probe state, environment overrides, and failure errors remain fingerprinted."
  "2026-08-24T17:38:55.072Z","harness:codex","Final correction evidence 2026-08-24: linked tests reran with trusted local-source provenance (10 transport + 4 fingerprint tests); nested objects named telemetry remain fully fingerprinted; endpoint, capture level, overrides, probe state, and failure errors all fail stale; enumerated direct queue/timestamp churn resumes. Authoritative full suite passed 572 files and 7,894 tests with exact 57,594/43,109/11,991/55,511 statement/branch/function/line coverage."
  "2026-08-24T17:42:43.295Z","harness:codex","Security Review finding: row names constructor, toString, and __proto__ could collide with inherited policy-map properties. The correction requires Object.hasOwn before resolving exclusions, so all prototype-like names remain fully fingerprinted and cannot crash normalization."
  "2026-08-24T17:50:03.583Z","harness:codex","Final prototype-safety evidence 2026-08-24: own-property lookup prevents Object.prototype collisions; constructor, toString, and __proto__ rows remain fully fingerprinted. Linked tests passed with trusted local-source provenance (10 transport + 4 fingerprint); authoritative 572-file, 7,894-test suite passed with exact 57,595/43,113/11,991/55,512 coverage."
  "2026-08-24T17:57:08.782Z","harness:codex","Final recurrence evidence: pnpm quality:static passed after the v3 health continuation policy and Object.hasOwn hardening. Bugbot final review reported no bugs; Security Review reported no actionable findings. Linked tests passed with trusted local-source execution: 10 real-process transport cases plus 4 fingerprint cases, covering lifecycle churn resume and stable, nested, and prototype-like negative controls."
  "2026-08-24T17:59:24.658Z","harness:codex","Delivery PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1108 at reviewed implementation head c855a5dd656c449a0fde5c0341dde0ff128f68d5."
  "2026-10-26T16:47:11.232Z","harness:codex","Hosted CI40351508407 coverage shard 3 timed out the existing health cursor replay fixture at 30 seconds. The fixture removed test suppression and enabled inline telemetry before its config command wrote the loopback endpoint, allowing the setup command to contact the default public collector. Keep telemetry explicitly disabled through config and endpoint setup, then enable it for both real health pages. Every original queue-growth, bounded-page, cursor replay and next-check assertion and the 30-second deadline remain. The adjusted real fixture passes locally in the 4.2-second transport suite; the original hosted failure is retained."
  "2026-10-26T16:49:58.307Z","harness:codex",The first linked replay was refused before executing either command because both immutable recipes originated on an older branch. Their exact commands were inspected and use the sandbox-safe repository runner. Acknowledge those existing recipes with the supported clone-local acknowledgement flag and rerun; retain the refusal receipt and keep trust policy/settings intact.
  "2026-10-26T17:52:10.877Z","harness:codex","The revised fixture explicitly keeps telemetry disabled through the config command and loopback endpoint write, then enables collection for the real health pages. Both linked commands pass after separate clone-local acknowledgement; 23 combined focused cases and the complete 11,461-test exact-coverage run pass with unchanged assertions and deadline. The complete log includes an expected failed-coverage diagnostic from the mocked terminated-gate unit test: a focused one-case run proves that diagnostic belongs to the intentional negative control, and the independent exact-coverage gate exits zero. The previously delivered cursor policy remains unchanged."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T17:52:11.715Z","harness:codex","Telemetry-enabled integration fixtures must bind their isolated collector endpoint before clearing the telemetry opt-out. A configuration command can itself trigger a flush after enabling policy, so endpoint setup after that command can leak synthetic events and couple tests to the public service."
